    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "When 2 TOX clients with empty friend list adds each other as '**no-request**',\n\nthe friendship will not be established.\n\nWhile when after that any of said client adds some other friend **with request**, the previous friendship is established right away.\n\nIs this know bug or some limit of TOX protocol?\n\nI know, that this is a corner-case, usual clients does not add any Friends without request, but it should be possible, right?",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This sounds like an edge case. However this should be covered by ci.\n\n`Autotox` supports a `LINEAR` friend graph, where only adjacent toxes are friended, via no request.\nBut I guess it means always adding 2 friends that way hmm...\n\nedit: This testcase specifically covers your case https://github.com/TokTok/c-toxcore/blob/master/auto_tests/friend_connection_test.c",
